# DropRevive Worker secrets: all optional. Deploy first, configure later.
# Nothing here is needed to deploy; LAN transfer works with none of them set.
# A drive turns on once its client ID, its client secret and DRIVE_COOKIE_KEY are all set.
# Leave a drive you do not use unset (or none).
#
# After deploy: Workers > your Worker > Settings > Variables and Secrets (type Secret), then
# open /setup on your site to check. Step-by-step guide: docs/self-host.md
# Locally: copy this file to .dev.vars (never commit it) and uncomment what you use.
#
# Google OAuth client ID (ends with .apps.googleusercontent.com)
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Google OAuth client secret
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Azure application (client) ID
# MS_CLIENT_ID=
# Azure client secret Value (expires within 24 months)
# MS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# 32 random bytes, base64 (openssl rand -base64 32); both drives need it
# DRIVE_COOKIE_KEY=
# Optional origin list, comma-separated, e.g. https://droprevive.example.workers.dev
# Unset: only this site's own origin (same-origin). Set it only to allow other origins.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
